y></table><table-wrap-foot><fn id="tfn14-ehp0115-000235"><p>Abbreviations: bw, body weight; F, female; M, male.</p></fn><fn id="tfn15-ehp0115-000235"><label>a</label><p>Exposures are calculated assuming species composition matches relative supply in the commercial seafood market; variability in measured Hg concentrations for each geographic region (imported, Atlantic, Pacific) and within each species was modeled using 10<sup>5</sup> Monte Carlo trials.</p></fn><fn id="tfn16-ehp0115-000235"><label>b</label><p>Modeled based on variability in CSFII data (1994&#x02013;1996&#x02013;1998) for each age group (<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b58-ehp0115-000235">U.S. EPA 2002</xref>).</p></fn><fn id="tfn17-ehp0115-000235"><label>c</label><p>Based on NHANES survey data 1999&#x02013;2002 (<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b43-ehp0115-000235">NCHS 2006</xref>).</p></fn><fn id="tfn18-ehp0115-000235"><label>d</label><p>Intake rates that exceed the U.S. EPA RfD for MeHg (<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b49-ehp0115-000235">NRC 2000</xref>).</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="t4-ehp0115-000235" position="float"><label>Table 4</label><caption><p>Modeled effects (mean and percentiles) of variability in Hg concentrations on potential exposure for women of childbearing age.</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><th colspan="7" align="center" rowspan="1">Modeled distribution of Hg intake (&#x003bc;g/kg bw/day)<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn20-ehp0115-000235">a</xref><hr/></th></tr><tr><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Fish meals/month<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn21-ehp0115-000235">b</xref><sup>,</sup><xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn22-ehp0115-000235">c</xref></th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Meal size (percentile)<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn22-ehp0115-000235">c</xref><sup>,</sup><xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn23-ehp0115-000235">d</xref></